{%- comment -%}
  One link destination out of `_data/**`, allowlisted and escaped. Liquid does not auto-escape and
  `_data/**` is attacker-influenced by pull request: `| escape` leaves the scheme intact, so
  `repository: javascript:alert(1)` reads as a URL in a diff and ships an executing link. data.rs
  rejects the scheme at ingest, but apps.yaml's `catalog` and `closed_source` links and a page's
  `redirect_to` never reach the scraper.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign href_s8 = href_url | slice: 0, 8 -%}
{%- assign href_s7 = href_url | slice: 0, 7 -%}
{%- assign href_s1 = href_url | slice: 0, 1 -%}
{%- if href_s8 == "https://" or href_s7 == "http://" or href_s1 == "/" or href_s1 == "#" -%}
{{- href_url | escape -}}
{%- else -%}#{%- endif -%}
{%- assign href_url = "" -%}
